diff --git a/mkdocs/development/auto_releases.md b/mkdocs/development/auto_releases.md
index 8a02ed6..ded6d53 100644
--- a/mkdocs/development/auto_releases.md
+++ b/mkdocs/development/auto_releases.md
@@ -147,6 +147,25 @@ the workflow checks if the current commit already has a release tag:
 
 If a tag exists, all subsequent release steps are skipped.
 
+## Preventing misplaced changelog entries
+
+A pull request can add an entry under `[Unreleased]` while another merge
+triggers a release. If the release rotates the existing entries into a
+versioned section before the pull request merges, Git can place the new entry
+under that version instead of `[Unreleased]`.
+
+To prevent this, pull requests validate `CHANGELOG.md` against their base
+commit. Changes are allowed under `[Unreleased]` and in comparison-link
+definitions. Version sections may change only when the change was generated by
+a release, which is detected from release tags and release commit messages.
+The comparison uses the merge base, so rebases and merge commits are handled
+by their final content rather than by commit-by-commit history.
+
+The auto-release workflow runs the same validation against the previous release
+tag before rotating the changelog. If an entry was added to an older release
+section, the release fails with a message identifying the misplaced entry
+instead of silently publishing it under the wrong version.
+
 ## Troubleshooting
 
 ### Auto-release didn't trigger after merge
